Cisco Packet Tracer - Connect to a Web Server

 Overview
This lab focused on observing how a client communicates with a web server using IP addressing and how packets travel across a network to reach a destination.
Although I already had an understanding of how **HTTP communication works**, this lab helped me focus more on the networking processes that happen before application-layer communication can take place.

The lab gave me the opportunity to use a client device to:
-Test connectivity to a remote web server.
- Observe ICMP communication using `ping`.
- Understand the role of ARP in initial communication.
- Analyze the meaning of TTL values in ICMP responses.
- Access a web server directly using its IP address.

Lab Environment
Simulation Tool: Cisco Packet Tracer
Source Device: PC0
Destination: Web Server
Web Server IP Address: `172.33.100.50`

